d just signing a petition or  calling your elected official I've said  before corporations have huge  disproportionate control over our  systems the legal system the judicial  system media everything they maintain  control in part by making sure that  there's a system in which the average  person doesn't go protest doesn't demand  change doesn't participate in strategic  defaults or mass rallies in urban  centers and one of the best ways to make  sure people don't do that that people  don't protest and people don't demand  change is if they can't even miss a day  of work  because that would be two or three jobs  that they might get fired from or they  can't miss a day of work because they  can't buy food if they miss that day of  work that's a really great way to make  sure people don't show up and actually  protest and demand real change and if  you're in a situation where you even  need multiple jobs then you are very  unlikely to have the wherewithal and  resources to go in protest and demand  changes to the system that caused you to  need two or three jobs in the first  place this is a self-reinforcing  feedback loop and I mean listen I don't  know the Fox News hosts who said it's  just so inspiring to live in a country  thank God we live in a country where  people can work ten jobs if that's what  they want to do they may be useful  idiots they may be actual cogs in the  wheel deliberately reinforcing the  system it doesn't really matter okay the  effect is that they are reinforcing the  system that big corporations have  already done a pretty damn good job at  reinforcing really disturbing and  disgusting stuff
 

